= The 2020 Primary

Two dozen candidates have entered. Only a few remain. The front-runners are a former vice president and a democratic-socialist senator. A South Carolina primary may decide it.

- @biden: Consolidate behind the former vice president.
- @open2: Let it play out.
- @sanders2: Back the senator.

@biden
subtitle: Electability argument.
on-arrival: nominee = "Biden"; estab_strength += 3; mod_strength += 4; prog_dissent += 4; unity += 3; nominee_mod += 0

Moderates rally. The race is settled by March.

@open2
subtitle: Lets the voters decide.
on-arrival: nominee = "Biden"; nominee_mod += 0.2; enthusiasm += 3; unity -= 1; prog_dissent -= 2

The nomination goes to the former vice president. The campaign was long but the left felt heard.

@sanders2
subtitle: Higher risk, higher variance.
on-arrival: nominee = "Sanders"; nominee_mod -= 0.2; prog_strength += 6; mod_dissent += 7; estab_dissent += 4; unity -= 3; far_left += 2; enthusiasm += 5

A rough, historic bet. The base is thrilled. The establishment is anxious.
